    {
      "type": "msg",
      "raw_time": false,
      "sender": "7ffeb8e03fcd49b682c67cd58fb5784f",
      "body": "Sync my Codespace with the class repo and push my work. Do not lose any of my work.\n\n1. Run git status. If there are any changed or new files, stage them all and commit\n   with the message \"save my work before sync\".\n2. Run gh repo sync. If it succeeds, go to step 6.\n3. If it fails because of diverging changes, do NOT run it again with --force. Instead,\n   run git fetch upstream, then merge upstream/main into my current branch. If there\n   is no remote named upstream, stop and tell me.\n4. If a notebook (.ipynb) has a conflict, do not edit inside the file. Keep my version\n   under the original name. Save the class version next to it with \"-new\" added\n   before .ipynb. Then mark the conflict resolved.\n5. Commit the merge.\n6. Push to origin.\n7. Show me a short list: files that came in from the class repo, and any \"-new\" files\n   you made. Stop after that. Do not delete anything. Do not force push.",
      "time": 1792424467.7265897,
      "id": "01f41591-8434-4d45-985e-28acef164035",
